{"sounds":{"intro":"Tajik is a form of Persian, written in Cyrillic with six extra letters. There are no genders and no articles. The stress is usually on the last syllable. Learn the special letters first.","rows":[["ӣ","a long \"ee\", like \"see\"","ман ҳастӣ"],["ӯ","a long \"oo\" with rounded lips, like German \"ö\" without the \"r\"","рӯз (rooz)"],["қ","a \"k\" made far back in the throat","қалам (kah-LAM)"],["ғ","gh, like a gargled French \"r\"","ғалат (gha-LAT)"],["ҳ","a breathy \"h\", always pronounced","ҳамин (hah-MEEN)"],["ҷ","j, like \"jam\"","ҷой (joy)"],["ё / ю / я","\"yo\", \"yoo\" and \"yah\"","ёр (yor)"]],"notes":["Tajik is Persian written in Cyrillic, so it shares most words with Persian (Farsi). It has no word order change for questions: the voice goes up."]},"numbers":[{"id":"0-to-10","title":"0 to 10","items":[["zero","сифр","seefr"],["one","як","yak"],["two","ду","doo"],["three","се","seh"],["four","чор","chor"],["five","панҷ","panj"],["six","шаш","shash"],["seven","ҳафт","haft"],["eight","ҳашт","hasht"],["nine","нӯҳ","nooh"],["ten","даҳ","dah"]]},{"id":"11-to-20","title":"11 to 20","items":[["eleven","ёздаҳ","yoz-DAH"],["twelve","дувоздаҳ","doo-voz-DAH"],["thirteen","сенздаҳ","senz-DAH"],["fourteen","чордаҳ","chor-DAH"],["fifteen","понздаҳ","ponz-DAH"],["sixteen","шонздаҳ","shonz-DAH"],["seventeen","ҳабдаҳ","hab-DAH"],["eighteen","ҳаждаҳ","hazh-DAH"],["nineteen","нуздаҳ","nooz-DAH"],["twenty","бист","beest"]]},{"id":"tens-and-big-numbers","title":"Tens and big numbers","items":[["twenty-one","бисту як","bees-too YAK"],["thirty","си","see"],["forty","чил","cheel"],["fifty","панҷоҳ","pan-JOH"],["sixty","шаст","shast"],["seventy","ҳафтод","haf-TOD"],["eighty","ҳаштод","hash-TOD"],["ninety","навад","nah-VAD"],["one hundred","сад","sad"],["two hundred","дусад","doo-SAD"],["one thousand","ҳазор","hah-ZOR"],["two thousand","ду ҳазор","doo hah-ZOR"],["ten thousand","даҳ ҳазор","dah hah-ZOR"],["one hundred thousand","сад ҳазор","sad hah-ZOR"],["one milli