"],["to spell","ҳарфбаҳарф гуфтан","harf-bah-HARF goof-TAN"],["to translate","тарҷума кардан","tar-joo-MAH kar-DAN"],["to graduate","хатм кардан","khatm kar-DAN"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Tajik has no gender. \"Ӯ\" or \"вай\" means he, she and it. Use \"шумо\" for one person you respect."],"rows":[["I","ман","man"],["you (informal)","ту","too"],["he / she / it","ӯ / вай","oo / vai"],["we","мо","mo"],["you (formal or plural)","шумо","shoo-MO"],["they","онҳо","on-HO"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ман донишҷӯ ҳастам","man do-neesh-JOO has-TAM"],["you are tall","ту қадбаланд ҳастӣ","too kad-bah-LAND has-TEE"],["she is my older sister","вай апаи ман аст","vai ah-pah-ee MAN ast"],["we are friends","мо дӯст ҳастем","mo DOOST has-TEM"],["they are teachers","онҳо муаллим ҳастанд","on-HO moo-al-LEEM has-TAND"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Add -ҳо to the noun (китоб, китобҳо). For people, -он is also used (бача, бачагон). After a number, the noun stays singular: ду китоб (two book)."],"rows":[["китоб (book)","китобҳо","kee-tob-HO"],["хона (house)","хонаҳо","kho-nah-HO"],["бача (child)","бачаҳо","bah-chah-HO"],["after a number: singular","ду китоб","doo kee-TOB"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","як хона, хонаҳо","yak kho-NAH kho-nah-HO"],["one book, books","як китоб, китобҳо","yak kee-TOB kee-tob-HO"],["one cat, cats","як гурба, гурбаҳо","yak goor-BAH goor-bah-HO"],["two books","ду китоб","doo kee-TOB"],["the children","бачаҳо","bah-chah-HO"]]},{"id":"to-be","title":"To be: ҳастам, ҳастӣ, аст","text":["\"Ҳастам, ҳастӣ, аст, ҳастем, ҳастед, ҳастанд\" are the forms of \"to be\". After a word they shorten: донишҷӯям (I am a student)."],"rows":[["I am","ҳастам","has-TAM"],["you are","ҳастӣ","has-TEE"],["he / she is","аст","ast"],["we are","ҳастем","has-TEM"],["you are (formal)","ҳастед","has-TED"],["they are","ҳастанд","has-TAND"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ман донишҷӯ ҳастам","man do-neesh-JOO has-TAM"],["you are tired","ту хаста ҳастӣ","too khas-TAH has-TEE"],["he is a doctor","ӯ духтур аст","oo dookh-TOOR ast"],["we are happy","мо хушбахт ҳастем","mo khoosh-BAKHT has-TEM"],["they are at home","онҳо дар хона ҳастанд","on-HO dar kho-NAH has-TAND"]]},{"id":"doshtan-and-hast-have-there-is","title":"Doshtan and hast: have, there is","text":["Tajik says \"I have\" with the verb доштан: дорам, дорӣ, дорад. \"Ҳаст\" means \"there is\", \"нест\" means \"there is not\"."],"rows":[["there is","ҳаст","hast"],["there is not","нест","nest"],["I have","ман ... дорам","do-RAM"],["I do not have","ман ... надорам","nah-do-RAM"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","ман бародари калон дорам","man bah-ro-dah-ree kah-LON do-RAM"],["I have a car","ман мошин дорам","man mo-SHEEN do-RAM"],["I do not have time","ман вақт надорам","man vakt nah-do-RAM"],["there is a problem","мушкилӣ ҳаст","moosh-kee-LEE hast"],["there is no water","об нест","ob NEST"]]},{"id":"present-tense","title":"Present tense: ме-","text":["Put ме- before the verb stem and add an ending. Рафтан (to go), stem рав: ме-рав-ам."],"rows":[["I go","меравам","meh-rah-VAM"],["you go","меравӣ","meh-rah-VEE"],["he / she goes","меравад","meh-rah-VAD"],["we go","меравем","meh-rah-VEM"],["you go (formal)","меравед","meh-rah-VED"],["they go","мераванд","meh-rah-VAND"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","ман нон мехӯрам","man non meh-khoo-RAM"],["you are reading a book","ту китоб мехонӣ","too kee-TOB meh-kho-NEE"],["she works in a bank","вай дар бонк кор мекунад","vai dar bonk KOR meh-koo-NAD"],["we drink tea","мо чой мениӯшем","mo choy meh-noo-SHEM"],["they are sleeping","онҳо хоб мекунанд","on-HO khob meh-koo-NAND"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb goes last. Order: who, where or when, what, verb. Tajik has no articles: \"китоб\" means \"a book\" or \"the book\"."],"rows":[["I read a book","ман китоб мехонам","man kee-TOB meh-kho-NAM"],["she drinks tea","вай чой менӯшад","vai choy meh-noo-SHAD"],["we go to school","мо ба мактаб меравем","mo bah mak-TAB meh-rah-VEM"]],"ex":[["I read a book","ман китоб мехонам","man kee-TOB meh-kho-NAM"],["he drinks tea","ӯ чой менӯшад","oo choy meh-noo-SHAD"],["we go to school","мо ба мактаб меравем","mo bah mak-TAB meh-rah-VEM"],["they eat bread","онҳо нон мехӯранд","on-HO non meh-khoo-RAND"],["the teacher writes","муаллим менависад","moo-al-LEEM meh-nah-vee-SAD"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put на- before the verb: меравам (I go), намеравам (I do not go). For \"to be\" use \"нест\" (is not). \"Надорам\" means \"I do not have\". Always compare with the positive form."],"rows":[["I go","меравам","meh-rah-VAM"],["I do not go","намеравам","nah-meh-rah-VAM"],["is","аст","ast"],["is not","нест","nest"]],"ex":[["I want","ман мехоҳам","man meh-ho-HAM"],["I do not want","ман намехоҳам","man nah-meh-ho-HAM"],["I speak English","ман бо забони англисӣ гап мезанам","man bo zah-bo-nee ahn-glee-SEE gap meh-zah-NAM"],["I do not speak English","ман бо забони англисӣ гап намезанам","man bo zah-bo-nee ahn-glee-SEE gap nah-meh-zah-NAM"],["I like it","ин ба ман маъқул аст","een bah man mah-KOOL ast"],["I do not like it","ин ба ман маъқул нест","een bah man mah-KOOL nest"],["she is here","вай инҷост","vai een-JOST"],["she is not here","вай инҷо нест","vai een-JO nest"],["I have a car","ман мошин дорам","man mo-SHEEN do-RAM"],["I do not have a car","ман мошин надорам","man mo-SHEEN nah-do-RAM"],["I understand","ман мефаҳмам","man meh-fah-HAM"],["I do not understand","ман намефаҳмам","man nah-meh-fah-HAM"],["we are tired","мо хаста ҳастем","mo khas-TAH has-TEM"],["we are not tired","мо хаста нестем","mo khas-TAH nes-TEM"],["he works on Sundays","ӯ рӯзи якшанбе кор мекунад","oo roo-zee yak-shan-BEH KOR meh-koo-NAD"],["he does not work on Sundays","ӯ рӯзи якшанбе кор намекунад","oo roo-zee yak-shan-BEH KOR nah-meh-koo-NAD"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Say the sentence with a rising voice, or begin with \"оё\". The word order does not change."],"rows":[["you are a student","шумо донишҷӯ ҳастед","shoo-MO do-neesh-JOO has-TED"],["are you a student?","оё шумо донишҷӯ ҳастед?","o-YO shoo-MO do-neesh-JOO has-TED"],["he is here","ӯ инҷост","oo een-JOST"],["is he here?","оё ӯ инҷост?","o-YO oo een-JOST"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","оё ин китоби шумост?","o-YO een kee-to-bee shoo-MOST"],["are they here?","оё онҳо инҷоянд?","o-YO on-HO een-jo-YAND"],["do you like tea?","оё шумо чойро дӯст медоред?","o-YO shoo-MO choy-RO doost meh-do-RED"],["is it cold?","оё сард аст?","o-YO sard ast"],["do you speak English?","оё шумо бо забони англисӣ гап мезанед?","o-YO shoo-MO bo zah-bo-nee ahn-glee-SEE gap meh-zah-NED"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words stand where the answer would stand."],"rows":[["what","чӣ","chee"],["who","кӣ","kee"],["where","куҷо","koo-JO"],["when","кай","kai"],["why","чаро","chah-RO"],["how","чӣ хел","chee KHEL"],["how much","чанд","chand"],["which","кадом","kah-DOM"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","номи шумо чист?","no-mee shoo-MO CHEEST"],["who is he?","ӯ кист?","oo KEEST"],["where do you live?","шумо дар куҷо зиндагӣ мекунед?","shoo-MO dar koo-JO zeen-dah-GEE meh-koo-NED"],["when is the lesson?","дарс кай аст?","dars KAI ast"],["why are you late?","чаро дер кардед?","chah-RO der kar-DED"],["how are you?","аҳволи шумо чӣ хел?","ah-vo-lee shoo-MO chee KHEL"],["how much is it?","чанд пул аст?","chand POOL ast"],["which book?","кадом китоб?","kah-DOM kee-TOB"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["Endings go on the noun: -ам (my), -ат (your), -аш (his / her), -амон (our), -атон (your, formal). To say you like something, use \"маъқул аст\" (it is pleasing) or \"дӯст доштан\" (to love)."],"rows":[["my book","китобам","kee-to-BAM"],["your book","китобат","kee-to-BAT"],["his / her book","китобаш","kee-to-BASH"],["our book","китобамон","kee-to-bah-MON"],["your book (formal)","китобатон","kee-to-bah-TON"]],"ex":[["my phone","телефонам","teh-leh-fo-NAM"],["your house (formal)","хонаатон","kho-nah-ah-TON"],["his sister","хоҳараш","kho-hah-RASH"],["I like music","ман мусиқиро дӯст медорам","man moo-see-kee-RO doost meh-do-RAM"],["I love football","ман футболро дӯст медорам","man foot-bol-RO doost meh-do-RAM"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["ту (informal): friends, family, children. шумо (formal): strangers, older people, work. Verb endings change: -ӣ (informal), -ед (formal)."],"rows":[["how are you?","аҳволат чӣ хел? / аҳволи шумо чӣ хел?","ah-vo-LAT chee KHEL / ah-vo-lee shoo-MO chee KHEL"],["you go","меравӣ / меравед","meh-rah-VEE / meh-rah-VED"],["your name","номат / номатон","no-MAT / no-mah-TON"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","аҳволат чӣ хел?","ah-vo-LAT chee KHEL"],["how are you? (formal)","аҳволи шумо чӣ хел?","ah-vo-lee shoo-MO chee KHEL"],["where are you going? (informal)","ту ба куҷо меравӣ?","too bah koo-JO meh-rah-VEE"],["where are you going? (formal)","шумо ба куҷо меравед?","shoo-MO bah koo-JO meh-rah-VED"],["please sit down (formal)","лутфан шинед","loot-FAN shee-NED"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: the past stem + person ending (рафтам = I went). Future: хоҳам + the short form (хоҳам рафт = I will go)."],"rows":[["I went","рафтам","raf-TAM"],["you went","рафтӣ","raf-TEE"],["he went","рафт","raft"],["we went","рафтем","raf-TEM"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","дирӯз ман хаста будам","dee-ROOZ man khas-TAH boo-DAM"],["I will study tomorrow","ман пагоҳ хоҳам хонд","man pah-GOH ho-HAM khond"],["we went to the park","мо ба боғ рафтем","mo bah BOGH raf-TEM"],["I saw him","ман ӯро дидам","man oo-RO dee-DAM"],["she wrote a letter","вай мактуб навишт","vai mak-TOOB nah-VEESHT"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal: бе- + the present stem (биё, come). Formal: add -ед (биёед). To forbid, use на- instead of бе-."],"rows":[["come (informal)","биё","bee-YO"],["come (formal)","биёед","bee-yo-ED"],["do not come","наё","nah-YO"],["sit down","шин","sheen"]],"ex":[["come here","инҷо биё","een-JO bee-YO"],["do not come here","инҷо наё","een-JO nah-YO"],["sit down","шин","sheen"],["do not sit down","нишин","nah-SHEEN"],["be quiet","хомӯш бош","kho-MOOSH bosh"],["do not be late","дер накун","der nah-KOON"],["open the door","дарро кушо","dar-RO koo-SHO"],["close the window","тирезаро пӯш","tee-reh-zah-RO POOSH"],["listen to me","ба ман гӯш кун","bah man goosh KOON"],["do not worry","хавотир нашав","kha-vo-TEER nah-SHAV"],["speak slowly","оҳиста гап зан","o-hees-TAH gap ZAN"],["wait a moment","як лаҳза сабр кун","yak lah-ZAH sabr KOON"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Can: метавонам + the verb (шино карда метавонам, I can swim). Must: бояд. Want: мехоҳам (бояд and мехоҳам are followed by the short form)."],"rows":[["I can swim","шино карда метавонам","shee-NO kar-DAH meh-tah-vo-NAM"],["I cannot swim","шино карда наметавонам","shee-NO kar-DAH nah-meh-tah-vo-NAM"],["I must go","бояд равам","bo-YAD rah-VAM"],["I want to go","мехоҳам равам","meh-ho-HAM rah-VAM"]],"ex":[["I can swim","ман шино карда метавонам","man shee-NO kar-DAH meh-tah-vo-NAM"],["I cannot swim","ман шино карда наметавонам","man shee-NO kar-DAH nah-meh-tah-vo-NAM"],["can you help me?","шумо ба ман кӯмак карда метавонед?","shoo-MO bah man koo-MAK kar-DAH meh-tah-vo-NED"],["we must go","мо бояд равем","mo bo-YAD rah-VEM"],["we must not go","мо набояд равем","mo nah-bo-YAD rah-VEM"],["I want to eat","мехоҳам хӯрам","meh-ho-HAM khoo-RAM"],["I do not want to eat","намехоҳам хӯрам","nah-meh-ho-HAM khoo-RAM"],["you can come","шумо омада метавонед","shoo-MO o-mah-DAH meh-tah-vo-NED"],["you cannot come","шумо омада наметавонед","shoo-MO o-mah-DAH nah-meh-tah-vo-NED"],["she wants to study","вай мехоҳад хонад","vai meh-ho-HAD kho-NAD"],["I must work today","ман имрӯз бояд кор кунам","man eem-ROOZ bo-YAD kor koo-NAM"],["you must not run","шумо набояд давед","shoo-MO nah-bo-YAD dah-VED"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Tajik uses little words in front: дар (in, at), ба (to), аз (from), бо (with), барои (for). The \"-и\" links nouns (izofat): китоби ман (my book)."],"rows":[["in / on / at","дар","dar"],["to","ба","bah"],["from","аз","az"],["with","бо","bo"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","китоб дар рӯи миз аст","kee-TOB dar roo-ee MEEZ ast"],["the cat is under the table","гурба дар зери миз аст","goor-BAH dar zeh-ree MEEZ ast"],["I am at school","ман дар мактаб ҳастам","man dar mak-TAB has-TAM"],["I am at home","ман дар хона ҳастам","man dar kho-NAH has-TAM"],["the shop is next to the bank","дӯкон дар паҳлӯи бонк аст","doo-KON dar pah-loo-ee BONK ast"],["the park is near the station","боғ наздики вокзал аст","bogh naz-dee-kee vok-ZAL ast"],["we meet in the morning","мо саҳар вомехӯрем","mo sah-HAR vo-meh-khoo-REM"],["the lesson is at nine","дарс соати нӯҳ аст","dars so-ah-tee NOOH ast"],["the key is in the bag","калид дар халта аст","kah-LEED dar khal-TAH ast"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add -тар to the adjective for \"more\": калон, калонтар. For \"the most\" add -тарин: калонтарин. \"Than\" is аз."],"rows":[["big, bigger, the biggest","калон, калонтар, калонтарин","kah-LON kah-lon-TAR kah-lon-tah-REEN"],["small, smaller, the smallest","хурд, хурдтар, хурдтарин","khoord khoord-TAR khoord-tah-REEN"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","калон, калонтар, калонтарин","kah-LON kah-lon-TAR kah-lon-tah-REEN"],["small, smaller, the smallest","хурд, хурдтар, хурдтарин","khoord khoord-TAR khoord-tah-REEN"],["this is better than that","ин аз он беҳтар аст","een az on beh-TAR ast"],["this is worse than that","ин аз он бадтар аст","een az on bad-TAR ast"],["she is taller than me","вай аз ман баландтар аст","vai az man ba-land-TAR ast"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Тошканд аз Самарқанд калонтар аст","tosh-KAND az sah-mar-KAND kah-lon-TAR ast"],["it is the cheapest","ин арзонтарин аст","een ar-zon-tah-REEN ast"],["the same as","монанди","mo-nan-DEE"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Quick sentences to copy and change."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","ӯ муаллим аст","oo moo-al-LEEM ast"],["you (plural) are students","шумо донишҷӯён ҳастед","shoo-MO do-neesh-joo-YON has-TED"],["I am happy","ман хушбахт ҳастам","man khoosh-BAKHT has-TAM"],["she is at school","вай дар мактаб аст","vai dar mak-TAB ast"],["you are my friend","ту дӯсти ман ҳастӣ","too doos-tee MAN has-TEE"],["it is cold","сард аст","sard AST"],["I study English","ман забони англисӣ меомӯзам","man zah-bo-nee ahn-glee-SEE meh-o-moo-ZAM"],["he teaches maths","ӯ математика таълим медиҳад","oo mah-teh-MAH-tee-kah tah-LEEM meh-dee-HAD"],["they work every day","онҳо ҳар рӯз кор мекунанд","on-HO har ROOZ kor meh-koo-NAND"],["is this your book?","оё ин китоби шумост?","o-YO een kee-to-bee shoo-MOST"],["are they here?","оё онҳо инҷоянд?","o-YO on-HO een-jo-YAND"],["do you like tea?","оё шумо чойро дӯст медоред?","o-YO shoo-MO choy-RO doost meh-do-RED"],["what time is it?","соат чанд аст?","so-AT chand ast"],["whose book is this?","ин китоби кист?","een kee-to-bee KEEST"],["how old are you?","шумо чандсола ҳастед?","shoo-MO chand-so-LAH has-TED"],["how do you say it?","инро чӣ гуна мегӯед?","een-RO chee goo-NAH meh-goo-ED"],["your book (formal)","китобатон","kee-to-bah-TON"],["their house","хонаашон","kho-nah-ah-SHON"],["my phone","телефонам","teh-leh-fo-NAM"],["excuse me, sir","бубахшед, ҷаноб","boo-bakh-SHED jah-NOB"],["please sit down (formal)","лутфан шинед","loot-FAN shee-NED"],["come here (informal)","инҷо биё","een-JO bee-YO"],["yesterday I was tired","дирӯз ман хаста будам","dee-ROOZ man khas-TAH boo-DAM"],["I will study tomorrow","ман пагоҳ хоҳам хонд","man pah-GOH ho-HAM khond"],["we went to the park","мо ба боғ рафтем","mo bah BOGH raf-TEM"]]}],"name":"Tajik","id":"tg","flag":"tj","note":""}